{{ tffile .ExampleFile }}

## Arguments Reference

* `identity_id` - (Required) ID of the identity whose work is reassigned. Changing this forces a new reassignment to be created.
* `config_type` - (Required) Work type to reassign: `ACCESS_REQUESTS`, `CERTIFICATIONS`, `MANUAL_TASKS` or `GENERIC_APPROVALS`. Changing this forces a new reassignment to be created.
* `reassigned_to_id` - (Required) ID of the identity that receives the work items.
* `start_date` - (Optional) RFC 3339 date-time from which work items are reassigned. When not set, the API default is used and kept.
* `end_date` - (Optional) RFC 3339 date-time at which the reassignment ends. When not set, the reassignment is permanent.

Dates that denote the same instant in a different format, e.g. with milliseconds or another time zone offset, do not produce a diff.

Changes of `reassigned_to_id`, `start_date` and `end_date` are applied with `PUT /reassignment-configurations/{identityId}` for the configured work type.

## Attributes Reference

* `id` - Resource ID in the form `<identity_id>/<config_type>`.
* `created` - Creation date.
* `modified` - Last modification date.

